  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2014-p16.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "By carrying out the multiplication, \\(8\\cdot\\underbrace{88\\ldots8}_{k}=7\\underbrace{1\\ldots1}_{k-2}04,\\) which has \\(k-2\\) ones.\n\nThe digit sum is \\(7+(k-2)+0+4=k+9.\\) Setting \\(k+9=1000\\) gives \\(k=991.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Multiply small cases: \\(8\\cdot8=64,\\) \\(8\\cdot88=704,\\) \\(8\\cdot888=7104\\)",
        "The product is \\(7\\underbrace{1\\cdots1}_{k-2}04,\\) whose digit sum is \\(11+(k-2)\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
